WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.700
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Intermediate.

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.177
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.477 --> 00:00:13.696
Unit nineteen: Finding a Home. In this unit, you will describe homes and talk about renting.

4
00:00:14.683 --> 00:00:15.394
tenant.

5
00:00:16.094 --> 00:00:18.825
tenant means a person who rents a home from a landlord.

6
00:00:19.125 --> 00:00:21.554
The tenant pays the rent on the first day of the month.

7
00:00:22.254 --> 00:00:24.094
Your turn. Say: tenant.

8
00:00:26.794 --> 00:00:27.551
tenant.

9
00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:29.423
deposit.

10
00:00:30.123 --> 00:00:33.644
deposit means money you pay at the start of a rental, returned at the end.

11
00:00:33.944 --> 00:00:36.129
We paid a deposit of two months' rent.

12
00:00:36.829 --> 00:00:39.191
Your turn. Say: deposit.

13
00:00:41.891 --> 00:00:42.823
deposit.

14
00:00:43.817 --> 00:00:44.655
lease.

15
00:00:45.355 --> 00:00:48.075
lease means a legal contract for renting a home.

16
00:00:48.375 --> 00:00:49.921
I signed a one-year lease.

17
00:00:50.621 --> 00:00:52.647
Your turn. Say: lease.

18
00:00:55.347 --> 00:00:56.278
lease.

19
00:00:57.283 --> 00:00:58.296
furnished flat.

20
00:00:58.996 --> 00:01:01.843
furnished flat means a flat that comes with furniture.

21
00:01:02.143 --> 00:01:04.445
A furnished flat is easier for students.

22
00:01:05.145 --> 00:01:07.414
Your turn. Say: furnished flat.

23
00:01:10.114 --> 00:01:11.359
furnished flat.

24
00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:13.618
utility bill.

25
00:01:14.318 --> 00:01:17.606
utility bill means a bill for electricity, water or gas.

26
00:01:17.906 --> 00:01:20.277
Our utility bill is higher in the hot season.

27
00:01:20.977 --> 00:01:23.699
Your turn. Say: utility bill.

28
00:01:26.399 --> 00:01:27.795
utility bill.

29
00:01:28.783 --> 00:01:29.924
spacious.

30
00:01:30.624 --> 00:01:33.134
spacious means having a lot of space.

31
00:01:33.434 --> 00:01:35.689
The living room is bright and spacious.

32
00:01:36.389 --> 00:01:38.995
Your turn. Say: spacious.

33
00:01:41.695 --> 00:01:42.719
spacious.

34
00:01:43.717 --> 00:01:44.451
cramped.

35
00:01:45.151 --> 00:01:47.766
cramped means too small for the people or things in it.

36
00:01:48.066 --> 00:01:50.170
The student room was cramped and noisy.

37
00:01:50.870 --> 00:01:53.232
Your turn. Say: cramped.

38
00:01:55.932 --> 00:01:56.701
cramped.

39
00:01:57.717 --> 00:01:58.718
location.

40
00:01:59.418 --> 00:02:02.056
location means the place where something is.

41
00:02:02.356 --> 00:02:06.085
The location is perfect: close to work and the market.

42
00:02:06.785 --> 00:02:09.159
Your turn. Say: location.

43
00:02:11.859 --> 00:02:12.941
location.

44
00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:16.100
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:19.668
I'm looking for a new flat. My room is so cramped.

46
00:02:20.983 --> 00:02:22.542
What about the one near the market?

47
00:02:23.850 --> 00:02:27.208
The location is great, but it's too expensive for me.

48
00:02:28.517 --> 00:02:31.712
Is the furnished flat near the university spacious enough?

49
00:02:33.017 --> 00:02:35.945
It's such a lovely flat, but the deposit is so high!

50
00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:39.830
Ask the landlord if you can pay it in two parts.

51
00:02:41.117 --> 00:02:43.476
Grammar focus: too / enough · so / such.

52
00:02:43.776 --> 00:02:46.739
Use too before an adjective when something is more than you want.

53
00:02:47.039 --> 00:02:53.662
Use enough after an adjective when it is sufficient. So goes before adjectives, and such a goes before adjective plus noun.

54
00:02:53.962 --> 00:02:58.435
For example: The flat is too expensive, but it's such a nice location.

55
00:02:58.735 --> 00:03:02.569
Enough comes after adjectives but before nouns: big enough · enough rooms.

56
00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:06.456
Now read and listen. Renting for the First Time.

57
00:03:06.756 --> 00:03:09.824
Renting your first home is exciting, but it can be stressful.

58
00:03:11.117 --> 00:03:13.650
Always read the lease carefully before you sign it.

59
00:03:14.950 --> 00:03:18.737
Check the utility bills, because some old buildings use too much electricity.

60
00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:23.617
Take photos of the flat when you move in, so you can get your deposit back.

61
00:03:24.917 --> 00:03:28.762
A cheaper flat isn't always better if the location is too far from work.

62
00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:32.412
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:32.712 --> 00:03:34.746
A person who rents a home is a blank.

64
00:03:35.046 --> 00:03:38.166
A, landlord. B, tenant. C, lease.

65
00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:43.871
The answer is B: tenant.

66
00:03:45.383 --> 00:03:47.360
The bag is blank heavy to carry.

67
00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:50.245
A, too. B, enough. C, such.

68
00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:55.762
The answer is A: too.

69
00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:58.924
He isn't old blank to drive.

70
00:03:59.224 --> 00:04:01.891
A, too. B, so. C, enough.

71
00:04:05.883 --> 00:04:07.616
The answer is C: enough.

72
00:04:09.117 --> 00:04:11.105
Having a lot of space means blank.

73
00:04:11.405 --> 00:04:15.081
A, cramped. B, spacious. C, furnished.

74
00:04:19.083 --> 00:04:21.222
The answer is B: spacious.

75
00:04:22.717 --> 00:04:26.249
According to the text, why should you take photos when you move in?

76
00:04:26.549 --> 00:04:31.572
A, to post online. B, to get your deposit back. C, to show friends.

77
00:04:35.583 --> 00:04:38.024
The answer is B: to get your deposit back.

78
00:04:39.517 --> 00:04:42.390
Now it's your turn to speak. Describe your ideal home.

79
00:04:47.690 --> 00:04:53.253
My ideal home is a spacious flat in a quiet location, close enough to the city centre.

80
00:04:53.553 --> 00:04:55.274
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:04:56.283 --> 00:05:00.294
Great work today! You learned eight new words and too / enough · so / such.

82
00:05:00.594 --> 00:05:04.384
Today's value is responsibility. Help at home and do your jobs.

83
00:05:04.684 --> 00:05:07.046
See you in Unit twenty. Goodbye!

84
00:05:07.346 --> 00:05:10.045
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

